.policy "fastapi-practice-cors-wildcard-with-credentials" revision 1
.description "Don't let a FastAPI or Starlette CORS middleware allow every origin while it allows credentials; list the allowed origins or drop the credentials."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule. Given `allow_origins=["*"]` (or an origin regex that matches everything) and
// `allow_credentials=True`, Starlette's CORSMiddleware answers a request from any Origin by echoing that Origin back
// with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` (starlette/middleware/cors.py: `send` calls allow_explicit_origin when
// `self.allow_all_origins and self.allow_credentials`, and preflights echo the Origin when credentials are on, as they
// do for every origin a regex fullmatches), so any website a logged-in user visits can
// send cookie-authenticated requests and read the responses. semgrep's wildcard-cors flags the literal only and ignores
// the credentials; Bandit and Ruff have nothing.
// The middleware is Starlette's CORSMiddleware (starlette.middleware.cors, fastapi.middleware.cors) or a subclass of
// the run, configured by `x.add_middleware(M, ...)`, `Middleware(M, ...)` (in `FastAPI(middleware=[...])`,
// `Starlette(middleware=[...])`) or `M(app, ...)`. Its origins allow everyone when `allow_origins`:
//   - is a list or tuple literal containing "*", or the string "*";
//   - is a name or attribute whose value, in this module or another one of the run, is such a value, or a `+` of
//     lists one of which is;
//   - is `os.getenv("X", "*")` / `os.environ.get("X", "*")`, or `x or "*"` (`x or ["*"]`), maybe followed by
//     `.split(...)` (an environment default);
//   - is `<settings>.F` where <settings> is an instance of a class of the run (`settings = Settings()`, or the
//     `Settings()` a function such as `get_settings()` returns) built without F, whose field F defaults to such a value
//     (`F: list[str] = ["*"]`, `F = Field(default=["*"])`, in the class or a base it inherits F from);
// or when `allow_origin_regex` is a regex that matches every origin (".*", "^.*$", ".+", "https?://.*", ...).
// `allow_credentials` must be `True`, or a name whose value is `True`. The options are read from the call's keywords
// and from a `**kw` whose value is a dict literal or a `dict(...)` call (`cors_kwargs = dict(allow_origins=["*"], ...)`).
//   app.add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, allow_origins=["*"], allow_credentials=True)              reported
//   app.add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, allow_origins=CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN, allow_credentials=True)  reported when
//       CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN = os.getenv("CORS_ALLOW_ORIGIN", "*").split(";")                       (an env default)
//   app.add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, allow_origins=[settings.FRONTEND_HOST], allow_credentials=True)  not reported
//   app.add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, allow_origins=["*"])                                       not reported: no
//                                                                                                 credentials
// Also left alone: values the rule cannot settle (a dict lookup, a call, a comprehension, a parameter, `self.x`), a
// settings instance built with the field or of a subclass that overrides it, a project's own regex (also a broad one
// such as "https?://.*\\..*": only the listed match-everything patterns count), a class that only shares the name
// CORSMiddleware, and test files. A wildcard under a dev-only `if` is reported: the branch's condition is not read.
// Gaps: a project's own CORS config objects (zenml's `CORSConfig(allow_origins=["*"], allow_credentials=True)`) that a
// framework later turns into the middleware; settings reached through a parameter or `self`; a settings validator that
// fills in "*" (zenml's server config); `allow_credentials` from a setting; positional middleware options; a value
// imported from a module of a namespace package (no __init__.py), whose module name the run takes from its path (the
// middleware subclass itself is matched there, below).

#include "lib/fastapi.rerail"

.violation CorsWildcardWithCredentials(at: node, arg: symbol) "`{arg}` allows every origin with `allow_credentials=True`, so any site can make cookie-authenticated reads. List the allowed origins; drop the credentials only if this public API needs no cookies."
.violation CorsWildcardDefaultWithCredentials(at: node, arg: symbol, src: symbol) "`{arg}` falls back to every origin (`{src}`) with `allow_credentials=True`, so any site can make cookie-authenticated reads. Default to an empty list, or drop the credentials for a public API."

// Values, settings classes and middleware subclasses may sit in other modules than the call (decision 0691: no node
// crosses files). Each file states its calls' options and its module variables' and classes' values in its own terms
// (cors_ev: settled there, or naming another module's variable, or a settings field); the relations over symbols
// below resolve those names, and the outputs read the answer at the call by its path and term (cors_place).

// ---- the middleware ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// cors_q(q): q is Starlette's CORSMiddleware, under either import path. cors_class(m): m names it or a class of the
// run deriving from it (lib/fastapi's fa_names, through the phase py_names).
.decl cors_q(q: symbol)
cors_q("starlette.middleware.cors.CORSMiddleware"). cors_q("fastapi.middleware.cors.CORSMiddleware").
.decl cors_class(m: node)
cors_class(m) :- fa_names(m, b), cors_q(b).
// cors_class_expr(e, ck, cq): e names the middleware, under condition (ck, cq) (cors_ok): ("", "") settled here; or
// ("ns", q): q is no such class here, but a subclass in a namespace package (a directory without __init__.py, as
// open-webui's `open_webui/utils/`) gets its module name from its path (`backend.open_webui.utils.asgi_middleware`),
// while the import names it from the package root (`open_webui.utils.asgi_middleware`): the import's name is a dotted
// suffix of the class's (cors_ns_ok).
.decl cors_class_expr(e: node, ck: symbol, cq: symbol)
cors_class_expr(e, "", "") :- unparen(e, m), cors_class(m).
cors_class_expr(e, "ns", q) :- unparen(e, m), sym_of(m, q), !cors_class(m).
// cors_call(c, ck, cq): call c configures CORS middleware with its keyword arguments, under condition (ck, cq). A call
// of a class the condition still has to settle counts only when it passes `allow_credentials` or a `**` splat.
.decl cors_call(c: node, ck: symbol, cq: symbol)
cors_call(c, ck, cq) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, _, "add_middleware"),
    call_arg(c, 0, "", m), cors_class_expr(m, ck, cq).
cors_call(c, ck, cq) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q),
    (q = "starlette.middleware.Middleware" ; q = "fastapi.middleware.Middleware"), call_arg(c, 0, "", m),
    cors_class_expr(m, ck, cq).
cors_call(c, "", "") :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), cors_class_expr(fn, "", "").
cors_call(c, "ns", q) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), cors_class_expr(fn, "ns", q), cors_has_opts(c).
.decl cors_has_opts(c: node)
cors_has_opts(c) :- kind(c, "call"), call_arg(c, -1, "allow_credentials", _).
cors_has_opts(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, s, _), kind(s, "dictionary_splat").
// cors_kw(c, k, ka, v): cors_call c passes keyword k as the keyword_argument node ka, with value v; also from a `**e`
// splat of a dict of this file.
.decl cors_kw(c: node, k: symbol, ka: node, v: node)
cors_kw(c, k, ka, v) :- cors_call(c, _, _), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, ka, _), kind(ka, "keyword_argument"),
    field(ka, "name", n), text(n, k), field(ka, "value", v0), unparen(v0, v).
cors_kw(c, k, ka, v) :- cors_splat(c, e), cors_dict(e, d), cors_dict_kw(d, k, ka, v).
// cors_splat(c, e): cors_call c passes `**e`. cors_splat_ext(c, q): e is a variable q of another module (its dict's
// keywords: cors_dkv, in its file).
.decl cors_splat(c: node, e: node)
cors_splat(c, e) :- cors_call(c, _, _), field(c, "arguments", al), child(al, s, _), kind(s, "dictionary_splat"),
    child(s, e0, _), unparen(e0, e).
.decl cors_splat_ext(c: node, q: symbol)
cors_splat_ext(c, q) :- cors_splat(c, e), kind(e, "identifier"), fa_ext(e, q).
// cors_dict(e, d): e is (or a name of this file holds) a dict literal or a `dict(...)` call d.
.decl cors_dict(e: node, d: node)
cors_dict(e, e) :- kind(e, "dictionary").
cors_dict(e, e) :- kind(e, "call"), call_name(e, "dict").
cors_dict(e, d) :- kind(e, "identifier"), fa_value(e, v), cors_dict(v, d).
// cors_dict_kw(d, k, ka, v): dict d holds keyword k (ka the pair or keyword_argument) with value v.
.decl cors_dict_kw(d: node, k: symbol, ka: node, v: node)
cors_dict_kw(d, k, ka, v) :- kind(d, "dictionary"), child(d, ka, _), kind(ka, "pair"), field(ka, "key", kn), str(kn, k),
    field(ka, "value", v0), unparen(v0, v).
cors_dict_kw(d, k, ka, v) :- kind(d, "call"), call_name(d, "dict"), field(d, "arguments", al), child(al, ka, _),
    kind(ka, "keyword_argument"), field(ka, "name", n), text(n, k), field(ka, "value", v0), unparen(v0, v).

// ---- values ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// cors_env_star(e): e is `os.getenv(X, "*")` or `os.environ.get(X, "*")`.
.decl cors_env_star(e: node)
cors_env_star(e) :- kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), sym_of(f, q), (q = "os.getenv" ; q = "os.environ.get"),
    (call_arg(e, 1, "", d) ; call_arg(e, -1, "default", d)), str(d, "*").
// cors_any_regex(s): an origin regex that matches every origin (Starlette fullmatches it against the Origin).
.decl cors_any_regex(s: symbol)
cors_any_regex(".*"). cors_any_regex("^.*$"). cors_any_regex("^.*"). cors_any_regex(".*$"). cors_any_regex("(.*)").
cors_any_regex(".+"). cors_any_regex("^.+$"). cors_any_regex("^.+"). cors_any_regex(".+$").
cors_any_regex("https?://.*"). cors_any_regex("^https?://.*$"). cors_any_regex("https?://.+").
cors_any_regex("^https?://.+$"). cors_any_regex("https://.*"). cors_any_regex("^https://.*$").
cors_any_regex("https://.+"). cors_any_regex("http://.*"). cors_any_regex("https?://.*$").
// cors_need(e): an expression whose value the rule reads: an option's value, a module variable's, a dict's, a
// settings field's default, and what those evaluate through.
.decl cors_need(e: node)
cors_need(v) :- cors_kw(_, _, _, v).
cors_need(v) :- fa_module_var(_, v).
cors_need(v) :- cors_dict_kw(_, _, _, v).
cors_need(d) :- cors_field_val(_, _, d).
cors_need(o) :- cors_need(e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", f), attr_of(f, o0, "split"), unparen(o0, o).
cors_need(s) :- cors_need(e), kind(e, "binary_operator"), op(e, "+"), (field(e, "left", s0) ; field(e, "right", s0)),
    unparen(s0, s).
cors_need(r) :- cors_need(e), kind(e, "boolean_operator"), op(e, "or"), field(e, "right", r0), unparen(r0, r).
// cors_ev(e, f, x1, x2, x3, x4): what needed expression e evaluates to, in its file's terms:
//   ("val", prop, how, src, ""): settled here: prop "true" (True), "wild" (origins that allow everyone: how "literal"
//     for the value itself, "default" for an environment variable's or a settings field's default; src the text
//     holding the wildcard), "regex" (a regex that matches every origin);
//   ("ext", q, "", "", ""): the value of q, a variable of another module (cors_var_val); "extw": the same, read as
//     origins only (split or added);
//   ("attr", rk, rq, a, set): `<o>.a` where o holds a settings instance: a call of rq (rk "call", set "1" when that
//     call passes a itself), or a variable rq of another module (rk "var") (cors_attr_wild).
.decl cors_ev(e: node, f: symbol, x1: symbol, x2: symbol, x3: symbol, x4: symbol)
cors_ev(e, "val", "true", "", "", "") :- cors_need(e), kind(e, "true").
cors_ev(e, "val", "wild", "literal", t, "") :- cors_need(e), fa_list_item(e, i), str(i, "*"), text(e, t).
cors_ev(e, "val", "wild", "literal", t, "") :- cors_need(e), str(e, "*"), text(e, t).
cors_ev(e, "val", "wild", "default", t, "") :- cors_need(e), cors_env_star(e), text(e, t).
cors_ev(e, "val", "regex", "", "", "") :- cors_need(e), str(e, s), cors_any_regex(s).
// `x or "*"`, `x or ["*"]`: the wildcard as the fallback.
cors_ev(e, "val", "wild", "default", t, "") :- cors_need(e), kind(e, "boolean_operator"), op(e, "or"),
    field(e, "right", r0), unparen(r0, r), cors_ev(r, "val", "wild", "literal", t, "").
// `<origins>.split(",")` and a `+` of lists: what is split or added decides, as origins.
cors_ev(e, f, x1, x2, x3, x4) :- cors_need(e), kind(e, "call"), field(e, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o0, "split"),
    unparen(o0, o), cors_ev_w(o, f, x1, x2, x3, x4).
cors_ev(e, f, x1, x2, x3, x4) :- cors_need(e), kind(e, "binary_operator"), op(e, "+"),
    (field(e, "left", s0) ; field(e, "right", s0)), unparen(s0, s), cors_ev_w(s, f, x1, x2, x3, x4).
// A name of this file: its value; one of another module: by symbol.
cors_ev(e, f, x1, x2, x3, x4) :- cors_need(e), fa_value(e, v), cors_need(v), cors_ev(v, f, x1, x2, x3, x4).
cors_ev(e, "ext", q, "", "", "") :- cors_need(e), fa_ext(e, q).
// A settings field: `settings.F` (`settings = Settings()`), `get_settings().F`, `config.settings.F`.
cors_ev(e, "attr", "call", cq, a, set) :- cors_need(e), attr_of(e, o, a), cors_ocall(o, v), field(v, "function", f),
    sym_of(f, cq), ((call_arg(v, -1, a, _), set = "1") ; (!call_arg(v, -1, a, _), set = "0")).
cors_ev(e, "attr", "var", q, a, "") :- cors_need(e), attr_of(e, o, a), fa_ext(o, q).
// cors_ev_w(e, ...): e's value read as origins: a wildcard settled here, or what another file settles.
.decl cors_ev_w(e: node, f: symbol, x1: symbol, x2: symbol, x3: symbol, x4: symbol)
cors_ev_w(e, "val", "wild", how, t, "") :- cors_ev(e, "val", "wild", how, t, "").
cors_ev_w(e, "extw", q, "", "", "") :- cors_ev(e, "ext", q, "", "", "").
cors_ev_w(e, "extw", q, "", "", "") :- cors_ev(e, "extw", q, "", "", "").
cors_ev_w(e, "attr", rk, rq, a, set) :- cors_ev(e, "attr", rk, rq, a, set).
// cors_ocall(o, v): o is call v, or a name of this file bound to call v.
.decl cors_ocall(o: node, v: node)
cors_ocall(o, o) :- attr_of(_, o, _), kind(o, "call").
cors_ocall(o, v) :- attr_of(_, o, _), fa_value(o, v), kind(v, "call").

// ---- settings classes, by symbol ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// cors_field_val(k, a, d): class k's own field a defaults to d (`a: T = d`, `a = d`, `a = Field(d)`,
// `Field(default=d)`).
.decl cors_field_val(k: node, a: symbol, d: node)
cors_field_val(k, a, d) :- kind(k, "class_definition"), fa_bind(k, a, d), !cors_field_call(d).
cors_field_val(k, a, d) :- kind(k, "class_definition"), fa_bind(k, a, c), cors_field_call(c),
    (call_arg(c, 0, "", d0) ; call_arg(c, -1, "default", d0)), unparen(d0, d).
.decl cors_field_call(c: node)
cors_field_call(c) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "pydantic.Field" ; q = "pydantic.fields.Field" ; q = "sqlmodel.Field").
// Stated in each class's file: cors_fdef(k, a, f, ...): class k's field a defaults to a value of form f (cors_ev);
// cors_binds(k, a): k binds a itself; cors_base(k, b): k lists base b; cors_cls(k): k is a class of the run.
.decl cors_fdef(k: symbol, a: symbol, f: symbol, x1: symbol, x2: symbol, x3: symbol, x4: symbol)
cors_fdef(kq, a, f, x1, x2, x3, x4) :- cors_field_val(k, a, d), cors_ev(d, f, x1, x2, x3, x4), class_def(k, kq).
.decl cors_binds(k: symbol, a: symbol)
cors_binds(kq, a) :- class_def(k, kq), fa_bind(k, a, _).
.decl cors_base(k: symbol, b: symbol)
cors_base(kq, b) :- class_def(k, kq), class_base(k, b).
.decl cors_cls(k: symbol)
cors_cls(kq) :- class_def(k, kq).
// cors_field_wild(k, a, src): class k's field a defaults to a wildcard (src its text), set in k or inherited from a
// base of the run that k does not override.
.decl cors_field_wild(k: symbol, a: symbol, src: symbol)
cors_field_wild(kq, a, src) :- cors_fdef(kq, a, "val", "wild", _, src, _).
cors_field_wild(kq, a, src) :- cors_fdef(kq, a, f, x1, x2, x3, x4), cors_ind(f, x1, x2, x3, x4, "wild", _, src).
cors_field_wild(kq, a, src) :- cors_base(kq, b), cors_field_wild(b, a, src), !cors_binds(kq, a).
// cors_inst(cq, k, sk): calling cq gives an instance of class k of the run, built by the call itself (sk "") or by
// the call def sk returns: a class, or a function of the run that returns `K(...)` (`get_settings()`), or a call of
// such a function.
.decl cors_fn_ret(fq: symbol, cq: symbol)
cors_fn_ret(fq, cq) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), fa_gives(g, r), kind(r, "call"), field(r, "function", f),
    sym_of(f, cq), pt_def(g, fq).
.decl cors_fn_sets(fq: symbol, a: symbol)
cors_fn_sets(fq, a) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), fa_gives(g, r), kind(r, "call"), call_arg(r, -1, a, _),
    pt_def(g, fq).
.decl cors_inst(cq: symbol, k: symbol, sk: symbol)
cors_inst(kq, kq, "") :- cors_cls(kq).
cors_inst(fq, kq, fq) :- cors_fn_ret(fq, cq), cors_inst(cq, kq, "").
cors_inst(fq, kq, sk) :- cors_fn_ret(fq, cq), cors_inst(cq, kq, sk), sk != "".
// cors_var_sets(q, a): module variable q is bound to a call that passes a. Stated in q's file.
.decl cors_var_sets(q: symbol, a: symbol)
cors_var_sets(q, a) :- fa_module_var(q, v), kind(v, "call"), call_arg(v, -1, a, _).
// cors_attr_wild(rk, rq, a, set, src): a settings field read so (cors_ev's "attr") defaults to a wildcard: the
// instance is built without the field, and its class (or a base) defaults it to one.
.decl cors_attr_need(rk: symbol, rq: symbol, a: symbol, set: symbol)
cors_attr_need(rk, rq, a, set) :- cors_ev(_, "attr", rk, rq, a, set).
.decl cors_attr_wild(rk: symbol, rq: symbol, a: symbol, set: symbol, src: symbol)
cors_attr_wild("call", cq, a, "0", src) :- cors_attr_need("call", cq, a, "0"), cors_inst(cq, kq, ""),
    cors_field_wild(kq, a, src).
cors_attr_wild("call", cq, a, set, src) :- cors_attr_need("call", cq, a, set), cors_inst(cq, kq, sk), sk != "",
    !cors_fn_sets(sk, a), cors_field_wild(kq, a, src).
cors_attr_wild("var", q, a, "", src) :- cors_attr_need("var", q, a, ""), fa_var_call(q, cq), cors_inst(cq, kq, ""),
    !cors_var_sets(q, a), cors_field_wild(kq, a, src).
cors_attr_wild("var", q, a, "", src) :- cors_attr_need("var", q, a, ""), fa_var_call(q, cq), cors_inst(cq, kq, sk),
    sk != "", !cors_fn_sets(sk, a), cors_field_wild(kq, a, src).

// ---- names of other modules, by symbol ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// cors_mv(q, f, ...): module variable q's value, in its file's terms (cors_ev). cors_dkv(q, k, kt, f, ...): module
// variable q is a dict whose keyword k (written kt) has such a value.
.decl cors_mv(q: symbol, f: symbol, x1: symbol, x2: symbol, x3: symbol, x4: symbol)
cors_mv(q, f, x1, x2, x3, x4) :- fa_module_var(q, v), cors_ev(v, f, x1, x2, x3, x4).
.decl cors_dkv(q: symbol, k: symbol, kt: symbol, f: symbol, x1: symbol, x2: symbol, x3: symbol, x4: symbol)
cors_dkv(q, k, kt, f, x1, x2, x3, x4) :- fa_module_var(q, v), cors_dict(v, d), cors_dict_kw(d, k, ka, e), text(ka, kt),
    cors_ev(e, f, x1, x2, x3, x4).
// cors_ind(f, x1, x2, x3, x4, prop, how, src): a value of form f (other than "val") is prop, how, src.
.decl cors_ind(f: symbol, x1: symbol, x2: symbol, x3: symbol, x4: symbol, prop: symbol, how: symbol, src: symbol)
cors_ind("ext", q, "", "", "", prop, how, src) :- cors_var_val(q, prop, how, src).
cors_ind("extw", q, "", "", "", "wild", how, src) :- cors_var_val(q, "wild", how, src).
cors_ind("attr", rk, rq, a, set, "wild", "default", src) :- cors_attr_wild(rk, rq, a, set, src).
// cors_var_val(q, prop, how, src): module variable q's value is prop, how, src.
.decl cors_var_val(q: symbol, prop: symbol, how: symbol, src: symbol)
cors_var_val(q, prop, how, src) :- cors_mv(q, "val", prop, how, src, _).
cors_var_val(q, prop, how, src) :- cors_mv(q, f, x1, x2, x3, x4), cors_ind(f, x1, x2, x3, x4, prop, how, src).
// cors_ns_ok(q): a class of the run deriving from CORSMiddleware has a qualified name ending in `.q`.
.decl cors_sub(q: symbol)
cors_sub(q) :- class_def(c, q), fa_class_names(c, b), cors_q(b).
.decl cors_ns_need(q: symbol)
cors_ns_need(q) :- cors_call(_, "ns", q).
.decl cors_ns_ok(q: symbol)
cors_ns_ok(q) :- cors_ns_need(q), cors_sub(q2), suffix(cat(".", q), q2).
.decl cors_ok(ck: symbol, cq: symbol)
cors_ok("", "").
cors_ok("ns", q) :- cors_ns_ok(q).

// ---- the rule ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Each call outside test code, by its path and term: its class's condition (cors_call_at), its options (cors_kv_at)
// and splats of another module's dict (cors_splat_at).
.decl cors_place(c: node, p: symbol, t: symbol)
cors_place(c, p, t) :- cors_call(c, _, _), docof(c, d), doc(d, p, _), pt_tm(c, t).
.decl cors_call_at(p: symbol, t: symbol, ck: symbol, cq: symbol)
cors_call_at(p, t, ck, cq) :- cors_call(c, ck, cq), docof(c, d), !fa_test_doc(d), cors_place(c, p, t).
.decl cors_kv_at(p: symbol, t: symbol, k: symbol, kt: symbol, f: symbol, x1: symbol, x2: symbol, x3: symbol,
    x4: symbol)
cors_kv_at(p, t, k, kt, f, x1, x2, x3, x4) :- cors_kw(c, k, ka, v), text(ka, kt), cors_ev(v, f, x1, x2, x3, x4),
    cors_place(c, p, t).
.decl cors_splat_at(p: symbol, t: symbol, q: symbol)
cors_splat_at(p, t, q) :- cors_splat_ext(c, q), cors_place(c, p, t).
// cors_kwok(p, t, k, kt, prop, how, src): the call at (p, t) passes keyword k (written kt) whose value is prop.
.decl cors_kwok(p: symbol, t: symbol, k: symbol, kt: symbol, prop: symbol, how: symbol, src: symbol)
cors_kwok(p, t, k, kt, prop, how, src) :- cors_kv_at(p, t, k, kt, "val", prop, how, src, _).
cors_kwok(p, t, k, kt, prop, how, src) :- cors_kv_at(p, t, k, kt, f, x1, x2, x3, x4),
    cors_ind(f, x1, x2, x3, x4, prop, how, src).
cors_kwok(p, t, k, kt, prop, how, src) :- cors_splat_at(p, t, q), cors_dkv(q, k, kt, "val", prop, how, src, _).
cors_kwok(p, t, k, kt, prop, how, src) :- cors_splat_at(p, t, q), cors_dkv(q, k, kt, f, x1, x2, x3, x4),
    cors_ind(f, x1, x2, x3, x4, prop, how, src).
.decl cors_credentialed(p: symbol, t: symbol)
cors_credentialed(p, t) :- cors_call_at(p, t, ck, cq), cors_ok(ck, cq),
    cors_kwok(p, t, "allow_credentials", _, "true", _, _).
.decl cors_literal_origins(p: symbol, t: symbol, arg: symbol)
cors_literal_origins(p, t, kt) :- cors_credentialed(p, t), cors_kwok(p, t, "allow_origins", kt, "wild", "literal", _).
.decl cors_some_literal_origins(p: symbol, t: symbol)
cors_some_literal_origins(p, t) :- cors_literal_origins(p, t, _).
.decl cors_literal(p: symbol, t: symbol, arg: symbol)
cors_literal(p, t, kt) :- cors_literal_origins(p, t, kt).
cors_literal(p, t, kt) :- cors_credentialed(p, t), !cors_some_literal_origins(p, t),
    cors_kwok(p, t, "allow_origin_regex", kt, "regex", _, _).
.decl cors_some_literal(p: symbol, t: symbol)
cors_some_literal(p, t) :- cors_literal(p, t, _).
.decl cors_default(p: symbol, t: symbol, arg: symbol, src: symbol)
cors_default(p, t, kt, src) :- cors_credentialed(p, t), !cors_some_literal(p, t),
    cors_kwok(p, t, "allow_origins", kt, "wild", "default", src).

CorsWildcardWithCredentials(c, kt) :- cors_place(c, p, t), cors_literal(p, t, kt).
CorsWildcardDefaultWithCredentials(c, kt, src) :- cors_place(c, p, t), cors_default(p, t, kt, src).

